
// Generated by Melissa Bianco's Almighty Fingers ver 9,000,000,000,002 on Thur Feb 5, 2008

//PLAQUES

//Cole Miner's Daughter
"PraetoriaTour3" "The majestic and timeless theatrical production called 'Cole Miner's Daughter', loosely based on the life and times of the Cole family before the end of the Dark Times, debuted at this theatre to great fanfare."

//People's Park
"PeoplePark" "<br><br><face heading><span align=center><color gold><scale 1.10><i>The Park of the People's Victory of Praetoria</scale></i></color></face></span><br><br><scale .6><face heading><span align=center><color gold>Dedicated to the patriots and bastions of Praetorian purity who gave their lives defending the world envisaged by and embodied within our most courageous Emperor Marcus Cole</color></face></span></scale><br><br>This plaque commemorates the location of Hamidon's first pivotal defeat in Emperor Cole's quest to bring peace and stability to the Earth.  This park now stands as a symbol of the Earth reclaimed from Hamidon and offered as a place of comfort, peace, and recreation for the people of Praetoria."

//Four Spans
"FourSpans" "<br><br><face heading><span align=center><color burlywood><b>The Four Spans</b></color></face></span><br><br>Bridging the southern fork of the Paragon River are the Four Spans; four bridges commissioned by the city of Praetoria and designed by our very own Emperor Marcus Cole: artist, engineer, and architect beyond peer. Each bridge represents one of the 'Four Guiding Principles' as outlined in <b>Emperor Marcus Cole's</b> seminal work of political theory: <i>"An Empire of the Mind"</i>. Each span also corresponds to the four volumes of <b>The Work:</b><br><br><b>1: Ideological Purity -</b> <i>An Open Mind is an Unguarded Flank</i><br><br><b>2: Moral Rectitude -</b> <i>Purity of Thought & Purity of Purpose</i><br><br><b>3: Dutiful Citizenship -</b> <i>Peace, Prosperity, and Submission to the State</i><br><br><b>4: Unceasing Vigilance -</b> <i>Friend, Family, Foe: The many faces of the Enemy</i>"

//TPN Campus
"TPNCenter" "<br><br><face heading><span align=center><color goldenrod><b>TPN: <i>The Total Praetoria Network</i></b></color></face></span><br><br>Founded by Praetor Tilman in the early days of the Empire, TPN started as a simple radio station broadcasting from a one room shack in Neutropolis, transmitting programs to inspire and entertain the people of Praetoria. In 40au Emperor Marcus Cole broke ground on what was to become the TPN Campus, equipped with high-power transmitters capable of spreading the Praetorian message across the entire world. None shall silent the righteous words of our supreme and enlightened leader: Emperor Marcus Cole."

//ViewCure
"ViewCure" "<br><br><face heading><span align=center><color gold><b>The Behavioral Adjustment Facility</b></color></span></face><br><br>Across these waters lies the Behavioral Adjustment Facility, where the unfortunate citizens who have succumbed to the effects of the Hamidon Spore are treated. Though no cure yet exists, those afflicted by the Hamidon Spore reside in the well-appointed facility, receiving treatment and living out their days in comfort until the cure is finally developed."

//Resistance Plaque 6
"Resistance6" "<face heading><span align=center><font color=pink>Lesson 6: This is the Cage and You're the Guinea Pig</span></face></font><br><br>Praetor Berry is the best propeller-head Praetoria has ever seen.  And you're the best test subject he's ever seen, too.  Welcome to your new life as a technologically assimilated lab mouse, chomper!"

//Resistance Plaque 7
"Resistance7" "<face heading><span align=center><font color=pink>Lesson 7: All That Glitters is Not Gold</span></face></font><br><br>Like jumpbugging around in a world where the streets are paved with gold?  Scratch that surface, chomper, and all that paint crumbles away showin' Cole's mug chortle-snortlin' in your face."

//Resistance Plaque 8
"Resistance8" "<face heading><span align=center><font color=pink>Lesson 8: Behavioral Adjustment = Thought Control</span></face></font><br><br>Gotta bugbump in your head and thinking of moseying up to the Behavioral Adjustment Facility for some attitude change?  Well, Cole has something in mind for you.  Your mind, which he's gonna scamp right out from outta your nose."

//Resistance Plaque 9
"Resistance9" "<face heading><span align=center><font color=pink>Lesson 9: Ghouls = Your Doom</span></face></font><br><br>They give you the shivery-wivveries every time you look at them, don't they?  It's because you're peeping something that's gonna happen to you if you don't stop Neuron Technology Unlimited.  It's unlimited, alright.  Can't make a 'perfect' omelet without breaking a few citizens, right?"

//Resistance Plaque 10
"Resistance10" "<face heading><span align=center><font color=pink>Lesson 10: There is No Mercy at the Psychiatric Hospital</span></face></font><br><br>Want a bowlful of brainbugs to slurp down in the morning?  Then head on over to that Hospital and join in with those smilies, the Seers.  How's that for a recommended daily serving of mercy for ya?"

//INVENTION TUTORIAL - CULTURAL DIRECTION AND EDUCATION CENTER

//Welcome Desk Pamphlets
"Praetoria_Invention_Center_Curriculum" "<br><br><face heading><br><span align=center><color greenyellow>Inventions Enrichment Curriculum</color></face></span><br><br><table><b><tr><td>Exercise</td><td>Title</td><td>Mentor</td><td>Location</td></b></tr><tr><td>Salvage</td><td><color CornflowerBlue>Recycling for Cole's Grandeur </color></td><td>Rupert</td><td>Resource Center</td></tr><tr><td>Recipes</td><td><color CornflowerBlue>Using Recipes That Make Cole Proud</color></td><td>Highland</td><td>Resource Center</td></tr><tr><td>Workbenches & Results</td><td><color CornflowerBlue>Materials + Inspiration = A New You</color></td><td>Frederick</td><td>Lab, Second Floor</td></tr><tr><td>Invention Enhancements</td><td><color CornflowerBlue>Inventing a New Mindset</color></td><td>Ross</td><td>Lab, Second Floor</td></tr><tr><td>Auction Houses</td><td><color CornflowerBlue>Sharing Circle</color></td><td>Chesterfield</td><td>Salon</td></tr></table><br><br><span align=center><color greenyellow>Approved by Emperor Marcus Cole<br>Cultural Direction and Education Center</color></span><br><br>"  

//Resource Center Bookcase - Loyalist
"Praetoria_Invention_Bookcase_L" "<face heading><span align=center><color greenyellow>Salvage</span></face></color><br><br>There are five types of Salvage, but the most common is Invention salvage. <br><br>There are three different types of Rarity: Common, Uncommon, and Rare. The color of the Salvage piece name, as well as information listed in the Information Bar, will tell you more about the piece of Salvage you are viewing.<br><br>You have a slightly limited Salvage Inventory that will expand with your Levels. You may 'store' your Invention Salvage at the Imperial Bank of Praetoria located in Nova Praetoria, Imperial City, and Neutropolis.  Salvage may be sold at any store or Trading House in Praetoria. You cannot buy Salvage from stores."

//Resource Center Bookcase - Resistance
"Praetoria_Invention_Bookcase_R" "<face heading><span align=center><color greenyellow>Salvage</span></face></color><br><br>There are five types of Salvage, but the most common is Invention salvage. <br><br>There are three different types of Rarity: Common, Uncommon, and Rare. The color of the Salvage piece name, as well as information listed in the Information Bar, will tell you more about the piece of Salvage you are viewing.<br><br>You have a slightly limited Salvage Inventory that will expand with your Levels. You may 'store' your Invention Salvage at the Imperial Bank of Praetoria located in Nova Praetoria, Imperial City, and Neutropolis. Salvage may be sold at any store or Trading House in Praetoria. You cannot buy Salvage from stores.<br><br><font color=pink><span align=center>[In faint lettering down below...]</font></span><br><br>Go to the Underground and buy and sell in safety without propaganda."

//Resource Center Visitor Console - Loyalist
"Praetoria_Invention_Visitor_Console_L" "<face heading><span align=center><color greenyellow>Recipes</span></face></color><br><br>Players have a Recipe Inventory, which is somewhat limited at first, but expands as players increase in Level.<br><br>Recipe Rarities are identified by color:<br><br>White = Common<br><font color=yellow>Yellow</font> = Uncommon<br><font color=orange>Orange</font> = Rare<br><font color=purple>Purple</font> = Ultra Rare<br><br>You can buy Common Recipes on the Workbenches, if you have the Information and room in your Recipe Inventory.  As you use Common Recipes over and over, if you meet the requirements, you can acquire special badges (based on Level and Type) that allow you to 'memorize' them.<br><br>Mousing over Enhancements shows a tool tip that gives you more information about that Enhancement.  Tooltips can be enabled and disabled from your Options menu.  There is additional text is displayed to show you exactly what your Recipe will build and what ingredients will be needed."

//Resource Center Visitor Console - Resistance
"Praetoria_Invention_Visitor_Console_R" "<face heading><span align=center><color greenyellow>Recipes</span></face></color><br><br>Players have a Recipe Inventory, which is somewhat limited at first, but expands as players increase in Level.<br><br>Recipe Rarities are identified by color:<br><br>White = Common<br><font color=yellow>Yellow</font> = Uncommon<br><font color=orange>Orange</font> = Rare<br><font color=purple>Purple</font> = Ultra Rare<br><br>You can buy Common Recipes on the Workbenches, if you have the Information and room in your Recipe Inventory.  As you use Common Recipes over and over, if you meet the requirements, you can acquire special badges (based on Level and Type) that allow you to 'memorize' them.<br><br>Mousing over Enhancements shows a tool tip that gives you more information about that Enhancement.  Tooltips can be enabled and disabled from your Options menu.  There is additional text is displayed to show you exactly what your Recipe will build and what ingredients will be needed.<br><br><font color=pink><span align=center>[The screen fills with words...]</font></span><br><br>Pro bono publica may mean 'for the public good', but guess who determines what 'good' is?  Cole."

//CreataVision Lab Visualization Console - Loyalist
"Praetoria_Invention_Visualization_Console_L" "<face heading><span align=center><color greenyellow>Invention Workbench and Results</span></face></color><br><br><font color=deepskyblue>Workbench:</font><br><br>Workbenches are used to build Items from Recipes.  They can be found here in the CDEC in the CreataVision Lab.<br><br>Click on the Workbench to interact with it.  Select a Recipe and click the 'Create' button.  If you do not have the required components, the Recipe will be unavailable (greyed out).<br><br>All Recipes are found on mobs or as rewards, but you can also buy Common Recipes on Workbenches.  You can acquire special badges that allow you to 'memorize' Common Recipes.<br><br><font color=deepskyblue>Results:</font><br><br>Recipes can build the following:<br><br>- Enhancements<br>- Costume Parts<br>- other types of Salvage (click on the Convert tab in the workbench window for choices)<br><br>You MUST have enough room in your Inventory in order to fit the results of your Recipe.  If you do not, the Recipe will display this and not allow you to create it.<br><br>Once a Recipe has been successfully used, the results will be placed in your Inventory.  The exception is Costume Parts, which will need to be 'picked up' at the Tailor's.  Lastly, you may only create a costume piece for the character you are currently playing."

//CreataVision Lab Visualization Console - Resistance
"Praetoria_Invention_Visualization_Console_R" "<face heading><span align=center><color greenyellow>Invention Workbench and Results</span></face></color><br><br><font color=deepskyblue>Workbench:</font><br><br>Workbenches are used to build Items from Recipes.  They can be found here in the CDEC in the CreataVision Lab.<br><br>Click on the Workbench to interact with it.  Select a Recipe and click the 'Create' button.  If you do not have the required components, the Recipe will be unavailable (greyed out).<br><br>All Recipes are found on mobs or as rewards, but you can also buy Common Recipes on Workbenches.  You can acquire special badges that allow you to 'memorize' Common Recipes.<br><br><font color=deepskyblue>Results:</font><br><br>Recipes can build the following:<br><br>- Enhancements<br>- Costume Parts<br>- other types of Salvage (click on the Convert tab in the workbench window for choices)<br><br>You MUST have enough room in your Inventory in order to fit the results of your Recipe.  If you do not, the Recipe will display this and not allow you to create it.<br><br>Once a Recipe has been successfully used, the results will be placed in your Inventory.  The exception is Costume Parts, which will need to be 'picked up' at the Tailor's.  Lastly, you may only create a costume piece for the character you are currently playing.<br><br><font color=pink><span align=center>[The screen flickers then fills with code...]</font><br><br>DG*CNGTV<br>DG*YCT*<br>DGNKGXG*PQVJKPI</span>"

//CreataVision Lab Visualization Console Sample Database
"Praetoria_Invention_Visualization_Console_Samples" "<face heading><span align=center><color greenyellow>Invention Enhancements</span></face></color><br><br>Invention Enhancements are a type of Enhancement that provides exceptional bonuses to players.  They can be slotted at 3+ a person's level; however, they cannot be combined with other Enhancements.<br><br>Invention Enhancements <font color=red>do not</font> expire as you increase in level.<br><br>The bonuses of any given Invention Enhancement is constant and based on the level of the Recipe at the time it was built.<br><br>There are new 'sets' of Invention Enhancements.  Each 'set' is made of single power Enhancements that, working together, give excellent bonuses as long as the single Power enhancements are part of the same 'set'.  <br><br>Other types of enhancement origins are Training (TO), which are the least powerful enhancement type, but are available to all origins; Dual (DO), which are twice as powerful as TO's yet only available to two origins; and Single Origin (SO), which are only available to one origin, but are the most powerful of the three."

//Museum Bulletin Board - Loyalist
"Praetoria_Invention_Bulletin_L" "<face heading><span align=center><font color=greenyellow>Trading Representatives</font></span></face><br><br>You are amazing.  You are wonderful.  You are just incredible, do you know that?<br><br>Emperor Cole believes you are the future of Praetoria.  As a Praetorian, you are under his wing, his protection from all threats, and he cares about you.<br><br>But are you as perfect as you can possibly be?<br><br>Don't you think you could be just a little bit better?  Stronger?  Faster?  More resilient?  Sure you do.<br><br>We can help!<br><br>Come visit the Trading House today in Imperial City. We are always open!<br><br>We can help you buy and sell those Enhancements that make you more you than you could ever believe (for a small fee, of course).<br><br>For more information speak to our Information Representative.<br><br><span align=center><color greenyellow>Approved by Emperor Marcus Cole<br>Cultural Direction and Education Center</color></span>"

//Museum Bulletin Board - Resistance
"Praetoria_Invention_Bulletin_R" "<face heading><span align=center><font color=greenyellow>Trading Representatives</font></span></face><br><br><font color=pink><span align=center>[There's a pamphlet with a chevron taped to the back of the recycle bin.  Someone's printed off a hard-copy of the Trading House advertisement...]</face></font></span><br><br>You are amazing <font color=dimgray>(ish)</font>.  You are wonderful <font color=dimgray>(for you, anyway)</font>.  You are just incredible, do you know that?  <font color=dimgray>(Probably because 'the propaganda machine' crams it into your head every day)</font><br><br>Emperor Cole believes you are the future of Praetoria. <font color=dimgray>(Oh he needs you all right.)</font> As a Praetorian, you are under his protection from all threats, and he cares about you. <font color=dimgray>(As long as you are useful)</font><br><br>But are you as perfect as you can possibly be? <font color=dimgray>(Clearly, you're not)</font><br><br>Don't you think you could be just a little bit better?  Stronger?  Faster?  More resilient?  Sure you do. <font color=dimgray>(In fact, you better!)</font><br><br>We can help! <font color=dimgray>(It'll cost you)</font><br><br>Come visit the Trading House today in Imperial City. We are always open! <font color=dimgray>(Go to the Underground if you value free will)</font><br><br>We can help you buy and sell those Enhancements that make you more you than you could ever believe (for a small fee, of course).<br><br>For more information speak to our Information Representative.<br><br><span align=center><color greenyellow>Approved by Emperor Marcus Cole</font> <br><font color=dimgray>(Tyrant! And a fraud!)</font><br><color greenyellow>Cultural Direction and Education Center</color></span>"

//CDEC - EASTER EGGS

//Pamphlet
"CDEC_Pamphlet" "<face heading><font color=pink><span align=center>[Someone's Idea of a Joke...]</face></font></span><br><br>How to Make Everyone Love You Without Having to Poison the Water Supply"

//Barf Poster
"CDEC_IPECAC_Poster" "<face heading><span align=center><font color=red>I.P.E.C.A.C.</font></span></face><br><br>Invention<br>Program<br>for the<br>Enrichment<br>of<br>Citizens<br>Adoring<br>Cole<br><face heading><font color=pink><span align=center>[Scrawled at the Bottom...]</face></font></span><br><br>NO one clued into the fact that the acronym is the name of a liquid that makes you throw up?  NO ONE?"

//Tyrant Poster
"CDEC_Tyrant_Poster" "<face heading><font color=pink><span align=center>[Sticky Note taped to the bottom of the frame...]</face></font></span><br><br>Ten Traits of Highly Successful Tyrants"

//Visualization Console
"CDEC_Visualization_Console" "<face heading><font color=pink><span align=center>[The visualization console flickers warmly, but you think to yourself...]</face></font></span><br><br>I'm just not seeing it."

//Bottles of Water
"CDEC_Bottle_Water" "<face heading><font color=pink><span align=center>[The bottles in this pack are still cold.]</face></font></span><br><br>Wait, this isn't minty.  It tastes like burnt almonds."

//Book - 10 Ways
"CDEC_Book" "<face heading><font color=pink><span align=center>[This book is surprisingly thick.]</face></font></span><br><br>Ten Ways That You, Too, Can Be As Amazing as Marcus Cole"

//Book - Individuality Sucks
"CDEC_Book_Individuality" "<face heading><font color=pink><span align=center>[A book catches your eye...]</face></font></span><br><br>Why It's Sometimes Better to Leave Thinking to the Professionals"

//Book - Cole Water
"CDEC_Book_Water" "<face heading><font color=pink><span align=center>[The folder on the counter looks technical]</face></font></span><br><br>100 Reasons Why You Should Drink Enriche, Cole-Approved Bottled Water"

//Bulletin Board - Studio 55
"CDEC_Advertisement" "<face heading><font color=pink><span align=center>[The notice on this board catches your eye]</face></font></span><br><br>Check out Studio 55 if you want a nightclub that is so fantastic it takes you to another dimension.  Seriously.  It really does.  We mean it.  No really."

//TRADING HOUSE - IMPERIAL CITY

//Stack of Papers Behind Reception Desk
"EE_StackPapers_01" "Someone's kind of messy."

//Primal Clockwork Plaque
"P_Primal_Clockwork" "<face heading><font color=pink><span align=center>Artifact #5865</face></font></span><br><br>This artifact is determined to be in existence on another plane.  Little is known about these robotic men, but judging from the crude workmanship, one would think them better suited to children's toys."

//Shadow Shard Ball Plaque
"P_ShadowBall" "<face heading><font color=pink><span align=center>Artifact #2255</face></font></span><br><br>This artifact suspends and turns on its own volition.  The craftmanship of the materials is unique and though it is encased in glass, there is a slight pulsing senstation as you stand near."

//Circle of Thorns Mouths Plaque
"P_CoT_Mouths" "<face heading><font color=pink><span align=center>Artifact #629</face></font></span><br><br>Ten Traits of Highly Successful Tyrants"

//Crates of Artifacts
"EE_Crates_01" "As you stand closer to this crate, you could swear you hear a scratching sound."

//Atlas Park Statue Picture
"EE_AP_Booklet_01" "This is a confusing image.  A man is carrying Praetoria on it's back, but he doesn't look like Emperor Cole."

//STUDIO 55

//Coat Check Computer
"EE_CoatCheckComp_01" "<face heading><font color=pink><span align=center>[The console hums quietly]</face></font></span><br><br>Please enter your item check number..."

//Glass on Counter
"EE_Glass_Counter_01" "<face heading><font color=pink><span align=center>[Used beverage glass]</face></font></span><br><br>You heard someone whispering that this was the glass Emperor Cole was drinking from earlier.  No one really believes it, but you've noticed it hasn't been touched in days and the odd person wanders by just to examine it (without touching, of course)."

//Enriche
"EE_Enriche_02" "<face heading><font color=pink><span align=center>[Enriche]</face></font></span><br><br>Well if people are just going to leave it sitting there, it's pretty much fair game."

//More Enriche!
"EE_Enriche_03" "<face heading><font color=pink><span align=center>[Bottles of Enriche]</face></font></span><br><br>You examine the bottles and note that they're still cold.  You're sure no one would mind if you took one.  They're sitting right there."

//Crate with Cole Logo
"EE_Cole_Crate_01" "<face heading><font color=pink><span align=center>[Official Praetorian Shipping Crates]</face></font></span><br><br>But they're just sitting there with no one to mind them.  That's either really silly.  Or...  Really sneaky."

//Condiments
"EE_Condiments_01" "Ha ha, very funny.  Someone loosened the caps on tke ketchup and mustard bottles."

//Jukebox
"EE_Jukebox_01" "<face heading><font color=pink><span align=center>[Jukebox]</face></font></span><br><br>Why is it all the songs are from decades ago?  And what are those black round things that spin?"

//Poker Chips
"EE_PokerChips_01" "Poker chips.  Unattended.  Well that just smacks of begs-to-be-stolen.  Good thing you're honest."
